        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: allow crabboxignore reinclude patterns",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Teach `.crabboxignore` matching to honor ordered negation patterns prefixed with `!`.\n- Add coverage for re-including a source directory named `target` while still excluding unrelated build output paths.\n\n## Why\nCrabbox's default sync excludes include broad names such as `target`. Some repos use `target` as a generated source package path, so they need a precise way to opt that source path back into sync without disabling the default output exclusions globally.\n\n## Validation\n- `go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestCrabboxIgnore|TestSyncManifest'`\n- `go build -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox`\n- Used the patched binary in Azure full runs for the Company Crabbox adoption test.\n",
